  106: "AI Affiliate",
  107: "★ Newcomers have the edge here",
  108: "I went through three markets — never a total loss, but never a real win either. Each one had its own wall, and I only saw it after hitting it hard enough to hurt.",
  109: "<b>E-Commerce</b> — selling products, running ads, optimising listings. Easy to get into, easy to convert, easy to measure. But commission is paid <b>once</b>, price competition is brutal, your capital gets stuck in inventory, and logistics eats the margin. It doesn't take much deep thinking — but you have to keep changing with consumer trends, forever. Stop running ads and the income stops. The most expensive lesson: <b>that income doesn't scale.</b>",
  110: "<b>Services</b> — content, consulting, coaching, running projects. Common in Vietnam and abroad, and you can start with zero capital. But this is an industry <b>for people with real expertise and real credibility</b>: easy to start, easy to open — but hard to run, and the costs keep climbing. It demands constant mental effort, competition is fierce, and scaling is hard before you have the capacity. More clients just means more work. I wasn't free — I'd only <b>changed bosses</b>.",
  111: "<b>Finance</b> — investing, stocks, forex, fintech. This one is <b>for the sharp and the capable</b> — it demands real intellect and emotional control. You need to be the marketer more than the player. Commissions are high, competition is moderate — but the risk is severe, the real value is thin, and it's genuinely dangerous for both the referrer and the referred when neither knows enough. I was just playing <b>gambling in a suit</b>.",
  112: "Chapter 1 · Selection Criteria",
  113: "WIN CRITERIA",
